# Repository workflow

- Preserve existing user changes; inspect `git status` before editing.
- Use the Orchestrator for multi-step implementation work.
- Delegate implementation to `dev` and independent verification to `test`; inspect the diff between them.
- Treat `yarn quality-gate` output and exit code as authoritative.
- Do not claim PASS when a required check failed or was unavailable.
- Stop after the initial attempt plus at most two focused fix-and-retest cycles.
- Do not commit, push, merge, deploy, or run destructive Git commands automatically.
- Report unavailable lint, unit-test, or integration-test checks honestly; do not invent scripts or dependencies.
- Read `renderer/AGENTS.md` before changing renderer files.
